WebKit: the curl NetworkCache::Data can share a mapped file with another process.

A content rule list (ENABLE_CONTENT_EXTENSIONS, LazyWeb+'s ad blocker, issue #845) is compiled
into a file, mapped, and handed to the WebProcess and the NetworkProcess as shared memory:
API::createExtension (APIContentRuleListStore.cpp) asks the mapped NetworkCache::Data for
tryCreateSharedMemory(). The curl backend defines that only for Windows (a file mapping
handle), so WebKit's UI process did not link with content extensions on.

On Unix-domain-socket platforms (LazyOS) the mapped bytes are copied into shared memory of
their own (SharedMemory::allocate: a memfd the SharedMemory owns, with its mapping), the copy
the other processes map. adoptMap is left as upstream has it: it closes the file's descriptor.
An earlier version of this patch kept that descriptor in every mapped Data, as GLib's backend
does, and wrapped it (issue #892): a NetworkProcess then held one descriptor per mapped cache
entry, on the way to fd_max, and the SharedMemory named the Data's descriptor and mapping, so
one that outlived the Data (a WebCompiledContentRuleListData copy outliving its
API::ContentRuleList, which destroys its mapped file first) would have named a closed
descriptor and an unmapped range. The copy owns everything it names and lives as long as its
last reference; it costs one copy of the compiled list in the UI process, made when a list is
compiled or looked up. Only the UI process calls this: ENABLE_SHAREABLE_RESOURCE, the cache's
other caller, is off in this port.

--- a/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/cache/NetworkCacheDataCurl.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/cache/NetworkCacheDataCurl.cpp
@@ -126,6 +126,25 @@
     return WebCore::SharedMemory::map({ WTF::move(newHandle), size() }, WebCore::SharedMemory::Protection::ReadOnly);
 }
 #endif
+
+#if USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
+// LazyOS: shared memory of its own holding a copy of the mapped bytes. It owns its descriptor and
+// its mapping, so nothing it names depends on how long this Data lives, and the Data keeps no
+// descriptor (adoptMap closes it, as upstream does: a mapped cache entry costs none, issue #892).
+RefPtr<WebCore::SharedMemory> Data::tryCreateSharedMemory() const
+{
+    if (isNull() || !isMap())
+        return nullptr;
+
+    auto bytes = span();
+    RefPtr memory = WebCore::SharedMemory::allocate(bytes.size());
+    if (!memory)
+        return nullptr;
+
+    memcpySpan(memory->mutableSpan(), bytes);
+    return memory;
+}
+#endif
 
 } // namespace NetworkCache
 } // namespace WebKit
